{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And he held his peace for her</b> — Two times in the Masorah: this one, and the other in the same parashah: <b>when her husband hears</b> (on the day he hears) <b>and holds his peace for her</b>, then her vows stand — this is what is stated in Nedarim: <b>when her husband hears</b> excludes a deaf-mute who speaks but does not hear, that he does not annul. And we learn this a fortiori from a husband [i.e., from the law of the father]."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The phrase וקמו נדריה ('her vows stand') appears to be the interpreter's paraphrase of the immediate context of the second occurrence (v. 8), inserted to identify it; retained literally. The final line וילפינן אב מבעל is rendered as 'we learn a fortiori from a husband' based on the standard reading of this passage, though the compressed syntax is somewhat ambiguous."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:28.838730332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}